        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-02T23:37:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This popped up incidentally in another thread, but without the explanation: &nbsp; Why does The Naturalist's Bestial Shift allow you to (essentially) play through the card twice? &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>I was playing a game against Akashbuta. &nbsp;Naturalist had out (among others) Natural Born Vigor, Natural Form's Power, and Cornered Beast, and had been gaining HP and feeding cards to other heroes, but I wanted him to start doing some damage. &nbsp; I played Bestial Shift, which in Gazelle Form reads: \"The Naturalist gains 3 HP. &nbsp;You may use a power now.\" &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>As I read the card, that would allow me -- in \"play a card\" phase -- to (a) gain 3 HP, then (b) use The Naturalist's inherent power to shift to Crocodile form. &nbsp;Then, in my \"use a power\" phase, between Vigor and Form's Power, I could use the Crocodile form's power and Natural Form both to do damage.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Instead what happened was this:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>(1) I played Bestial Shift.</span></p><p><span>(2) Naturalist gained 3 HP.</span></p><p><span>(3) The game let me use a power, so I shifted to Crocodile Form (got it out of the trash). &nbsp;</span></p><p><span>(4) Naturalist dealt 3 (+1) toxic damage, via the Crocodile text on Bestial Shift (\"The Naturalist deals 3 toxic damage. &nbsp;You may use a power now.\")</span></p><p><span>(5) Still in \"Play a card\" phase, the game allowed me to use a power -- I used Crocodile Form's power to do 2 (+1) melee damage. &nbsp;</span></p><p><span>(6) The game then shifted to \"Use a power\" phase.</span></p><p><span>(7) I used Natural Form's power to deal 1 + 1 toxic damage to two different targets.</span></p><p><span>(8) The game gave me the option to use Cornered Beast's power, but there were no targets under 3HP to destroy, so I just pressed \"Skip,\" and ended Naturalist's turn.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>What is the game mechanism that essentially repeats Bestial Shift's operation once you switch forms? &nbsp; Not that I'm complaining by any means, but b</span><span>y my count, the game allowed me four power usages: &nbsp;</span></p><p><span>(1) Naturalist's inherent power, upon playing Bestial Shift in Gazelle form;</span></p><p><span>(2) Crocodile form's power</span></p><p><span>(3) Natural Form's \"Crocodile\" power, and&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>(4) Cornered Beast.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:36.729Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
