        "raw": "<p>This popped up incidentally in another thread, but without the explanation: &nbsp; Why does The Naturalist&#39;s Bestial Shift allow you to (essentially) play through the card twice? &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">I was playing a game against Akashbuta. &nbsp;Naturalist had out (among others) Natural Born Vigor, Natural Form&#39;s Power, and Cornered Beast, and had been gaining HP and feeding cards to other heroes, but I wanted him to start doing some damage. &nbsp; I played Bestial Shift, which in Gazelle Form reads: &quot;The Naturalist gains 3 HP. &nbsp;You may use a power now.&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">As I read the card, that would allow me -- in &quot;play a card&quot; phase -- to (a) gain 3 HP, then (b) use The Naturalist&#39;s inherent power to shift to Crocodile form. &nbsp;Then, in my &quot;use a power&quot; phase, between Vigor and Form&#39;s Power, I could use the Crocodile form&#39;s power and Natural Form both to do damage.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Instead what happened was this:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(1) I played Bestial Shift.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(2) Naturalist gained 3 HP.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(3) The game let me use a power, so I shifted to Crocodile Form (got it out of the trash). &nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(4) Naturalist dealt 3 (+1) toxic damage, via the Crocodile text on Bestial Shift (&quot;The Naturalist deals 3 toxic damage. &nbsp;You may use a power now.&quot;)</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(5) Still in &quot;Play a card&quot; phase, the game allowed me to use a power -- I used Crocodile Form&#39;s power to do 2 (+1) melee damage. &nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(6) The game then shifted to &quot;Use a power&quot; phase.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(7) I used Natural Form&#39;s power to deal 1 + 1 toxic damage to two different targets.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(8) The game gave me the option to use Cornered Beast&#39;s power, but there were no targets under 3HP to destroy, so I just pressed &quot;Skip,&quot; and ended Naturalist&#39;s turn.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">What is the game mechanism that essentially repeats Bestial Shift&#39;s operation once you switch forms? &nbsp; Not that I&#39;m complaining by any means, but b</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">y my count, the game allowed me four power usages: &nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(1) Naturalist&#39;s inherent power, upon playing Bestial Shift in Gazelle form;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(2) Crocodile form&#39;s power</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(3) Natural Form&#39;s &quot;Crocodile&quot; power, and&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(4) Cornered Beast.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
